 <blockquote class="text-slate-700 text-base italic leading-relaxed">"USB Power Delivery 3.1 marks the single largest power increase in the USB specification's history, from 100W to 240W, by introducing Extended Power Range (EPR) with new 28V, 36V, and 48V fixed voltage levels. The EU's Common Charger Directive mandating USB-C for laptops from April 2026 makes PD 3.1 EPR compliance a de facto requirement for any charger targeting the European laptop market."</blockquote>
 <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 mt-2">, USB-IF Power Delivery 3.1 Specification v1.8 & EU Directive 2022/2380 (Common Charger Directive)</p>
